  "scope": "Measurement only: no calculations are skipped. Every instrumented solver row is identical to the archived item-projection solver after removing the census and wall times, with two runs per backend. Each measured cell is bound to the archived native outcome audit by guarded state identity and joint choices. Raw and existing guarded keys are compared with a candidate which removes unselected current/base moves of active Pokemon only when the chosen move is not Sleep Talk; existing damage and Quick Claw guards are retained unchanged. HP, items, conditions and other state fields remain. A deliberately unsafe key also discards the Sleep Talk pool and produces outcome conflicts. Observed agreement of the candidate does not prove equivalence on every state. Potential saved runs count repeated cells on this fixed computation schedule, exclude key-building and cache costs, and are not a measured speedup. This census alone does not establish enough runtime savings to reach 500ms. No cache or production integration is adopted here."
